    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_853c2632",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: stand-your-ground-law-meme; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts a man in a mugshot pose holding a blank card, with text that reads 'stand your ground law.' and 'i said \"nibber get\"'. The juxtaposition of the 'stand your ground' legal concept with the absurd, possibly racially charged phrase 'nibber get' (a derogatory term often used to refer to Black people, implying a stereotypical criminal behavior association) is intended to mock or satirize the law. The visual of the mugshot reinforces the idea of criminality. While not explicitly abusive or hateful toward a specific individual, the use of a racial slur and the implication of criminal behavior associated with a racial group makes the meme harmful. It perpetuates a stereotype by linking a legal principle to a racially charged, derogatory phrase, potentially reinforcing negative racial biases and contributing to a hostile environment for the targeted group. The intent is to provoke laughter through shock value and the absurdity of the combination, but this comes at the cost of reinforcing harmful stereotypes.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_3f857e67"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
