    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_3010d997",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target audience is individuals familiar with U.S. legal concepts, particularly the 'stand your ground' law, and who are aware of or have encountered racial slurs like 'nibber get' in internet or media contexts. The meme is designed to provoke laughter through shock value and absurdity, likely appealing to an audience that finds humor in satirical juxtapositions involving law enforcement, criminal stereotypes, and racially charged language. This audience may include internet users who engage with satirical or dark humor memes, particularly those who understand the historical context of anti-Black stereotypes and the legal doctrine being mocked. The visual of the mugshot and the text 'stand your ground law' combined with 'nibber get' suggest the meme targets those who are culturally literate enough to recognize the irony and the underlying racial insensitivity, and who may be part of online communities that share or create memes that use offensive language for comedic effect, despite the harmful implications.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
